# ── Contact form (footer "Let's Talk Bam") ──────────────────────────────────
# Without these the form renders and validates, but returns a clear
# "not configured yet" error instead of silently pretending to send.
#
# 1. Create an account at https://resend.com and verify the hypebam.lk domain
#    (add the DNS records it gives you).
# 2. Create an API key and paste it here.
# 3. Add BOTH values in Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables.

RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Must be an address on the domain you verified above.
CONTACT_FROM=Hype Bam <website@hypebam.lk>

# Optional — comma-separated. Defaults to info@hypebam.lk,sales@hypebam.lk
# CONTACT_TO=info@hypebam.lk,sales@hypebam.lk


# ── SECURITY NOTES ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WHY THIS IS SAFE: RESEND_API_KEY has no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, so Next.js never
# inlines it into the browser bundle. It is read at request time inside the
# server-only Route Handler (src/app/api/contact/route.ts). The browser's only
# network call is a same-origin POST to /api/contact — it never sees the key,
# and the key is never baked into any build artifact (verified by building with
# a sentinel value and grepping .next/static + the rendered HTML: zero hits).
#
# NEVER prefix a secret with NEXT_PUBLIC_ — that is the one change that would
# publish it to every visitor.
#
# Keep .env out of git (it is gitignored). Store the real values only in
# Vercel's encrypted environment variables. If a key is ever pasted into a
# commit, screenshot, or chat, rotate it in the Resend dashboard immediately —
# rotation is cheap, and a leaked key lets anyone send mail as your domain.
#
# ABUSE PROTECTION currently in the route: same-origin check, honeypot field,
# minimum dwell time, body-size cap, and a best-effort per-IP rate limit. That
# rate limit is per serverless instance, so it is not a hard global cap — if
# real spam ever appears, escalate to a shared store (Vercel KV / Upstash) or
# add Cloudflare Turnstile. Note Turnstile loads a third-party script, so it
# would also require adding challenges.cloudflare.com to script-src in the CSP
# in next.config.ts — the site is otherwise deliberately 100% self-hosted.
#
# DELIVERABILITY: verify hypebam.lk in Resend and add its SPF + DKIM records
# (and ideally a DMARC record). Without them, mail from your own domain lands
# in spam — which for a brand contact form is a silent, expensive failure.
